# Sign-on (SSO)

The web UI authenticates through Airflow's **FAB auth manager**, configured
in `airflow/config/webserver_config.py` (mounted into the api-server).
{{#if withEntraId}}This project was scaffolded with **Microsoft Entra ID**
sign-on.{{else}}This project was scaffolded with the **native** sign-on
(Airflow user database).{{/if}}

## Native (user database)

Users, passwords and role assignments live in Airflow's own database, managed
under **Security → Users** in the UI or via CLI:

```bash
docker compose run --rm airflow-cli airflow users create \
  --role Viewer --username jane --password … \
  --firstname Jane --lastname Doe --email jane@example.com
```

{{#unless withEntraId}}
The first admin is created automatically on `dude up` from
`AIRFLOW_ADMIN_USERNAME` / `AIRFLOW_ADMIN_PASSWORD` in `.env` — **change the
defaults before exposing the UI anywhere**.
{{/unless}}

## Microsoft Entra ID (OAuth 2.0 / OIDC)

{{#if withEntraId}}
Already enabled — finish the setup on the Entra side:
{{else}}
To switch, edit `airflow/config/webserver_config.py` (replace the `AUTH_DB`
block with the `AUTH_OAUTH` one — scaffold a throwaway project with
`--sso entra-id` to copy it), add `authlib` to `airflow/requirements.txt`,
provide the variables below in `.env`, then `dude up --build`. On the Entra
side:
{{/if}}

1. **App registration** (Entra admin center → App registrations → New):
   - Redirect URI (Web): `http://localhost:8080/auth/oauth-authorized/azure`
     — add your production URL alongside it after deploying
     (`https://<host>/auth/oauth-authorized/azure`).
   - Create a **client secret** (Certificates & secrets).
2. **App roles** (App roles → Create): create `airflow_admin`, `airflow_op`,
   `airflow_user`, `airflow_viewer` (value = display name), then assign them
   to users/groups under *Enterprise applications → your app → Users and
   groups*. `AUTH_ROLES_MAPPING` in `webserver_config.py` maps them onto
   Airflow's Admin / Op / User / Viewer roles at every login
   (`AUTH_ROLES_SYNC_AT_LOGIN`).
3. **Configuration** — fill in `.env` (locally; in AWS use
   `dude iac secrets`):

   | Variable | Where to find it |
   | -------- | ---------------- |
   | `AZURE_TENANT_ID` | App overview → Directory (tenant) ID |
   | `AZURE_CLIENT_ID` | App overview → Application (client) ID |
   | `AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET` | The secret created in step 1 |
   | `AUTH_USER_REGISTRATION_ROLE` | Role for users with no mapped app role (default `Viewer`) |

Users without any assigned app role are auto-registered with
`AUTH_USER_REGISTRATION_ROLE` — set it to a harmless role (`Viewer`) or
restrict the enterprise app to assigned users only.

## Roles cheat-sheet

| Airflow role | Can |
| ------------ | --- |
| `Admin` | everything, incl. Security and Connections |
| `Op` | trigger/clear DAGs + edit Connections/Variables/Pools |
| `User` | trigger/clear DAGs |
| `Viewer` | read-only |
